{
  "title": "Consumer setup step 5: add init command",
  "description": "Step 5 of the consumer setup sequence, after shared docs, \
skills, and hook behavior have stable targets. Add an agent-issues bootstrap \
command for consumer repositories. It should create or update only minimal \
scaffolding such as an issues/.gitignore that keeps an otherwise-empty issue \
directory present using * and !.gitignore patterns, optional AGENTS.md and \
CLAUDE.md includes, optional local skill-note templates, optional hook \
settings, and optional Makefile or CI snippets. The command should support \
dry-run output, detect existing files, avoid overwriting non-generated \
content, and keep generated setup PRs small. It should be suitable for future \
repos and for auditing library-of-leng, infallible-record, and ramekin \
migrations.",
